@talks mensah
// TW1, the Talk a while pack: Kofi Mensah's own talks (he/him). Senior Watch Officer, nights. Big easy laugh, eyes
// always moving; calls the ship "she"; tells a story slowly and lands it; keeps a count of Holt's laughs. Never
// repeats what Holt tells him in confidence.

== good-night
topic: ship
them: Ha! You caught me. I say good night to every deck on my rounds. By name.
them: "Night, Three. Night, Garden." She likes it. I'm sure she likes it.   #funny
ask: Do you have a little habit like that? Something just for you?
listen: Does any deck answer back?
  them: Six hums. Every time. I take that as a good night back.   #warm
share: I tap the bunk ladder twice before bed.
  them: Good. Keep it. Little habits are how you tell a ship you live here.   #warm
cheer: I say good morning to the toaster.
  them: Then the toaster's in good hands. Nights and mornings, covered.   #funny

== the-count
topic: crew
when: tier>=acquaintance
them: I keep a count. How many times I've made Holt laugh. Proper laughs. No snorts.
them: I won't tell you the number. He'd find out. He finds everything out.   #funny
ask: Who's the hardest person you've made laugh?
listen: What was the best one?
  them: One about a kettle. Long story, short punchline. Three whole seconds, he laughed.   #funny
share: Someone back home. Took me years.
  them: Then you know the feeling. Worth every year, those laughs.   #warm
cheer: Chief Calder. Once. By accident.
  them: Calder? Ha! Write it down. Date it. Nobody will believe you otherwise.   #funny

== night-watch
topic: work
when: tier>=colleague
them: Nights are a different ship. Quiet. The lights low. Everybody's door shut and safe.
them: That's my job, really. Being awake so the rest of you don't have to be.
ask: Would you ever work nights, do you think?
listen: Don't you miss the daytime?
  them: Sometimes. Breakfast with the day crew. I get it as dinner. Funny old life.   #funny
share: Maybe. The quiet sounds nice.
  them: It is. The ship talks more at night. Softly. You'd hear it.   #warm
cheer: Only if there's a night-time breakfast.
  them: Ha! There is. Six sharp. Brennan feeds the night lot first. Best kept secret aboard.   #funny

== watching
topic: day
when: tier>=friend
them: Here's a thing about the Watch. You watch people, too. Not just doors.
them: Who's eating. Who's quiet. Who laughs too loud. Then you send someone kind. Or go.   #warm
ask: Who looks out for you, when you're not all right?
listen: And who watches the watcher?
  them: Holt. He'd never say it. He just turns up with tea he doesn't like.   #warm
share: A few people now. You, maybe.
  them: Me? Always. That's a promise, that. Write it down with the Holt count.   #warm
cheer: Whoever left the light on for me.
  them: Fair. A light left on is the ship's kindest habit.   #warm
